(*
expect:
true
true
true
true
done
*)
(* rete#224 — `platform monotonicMillis` past the SMI band answers a POSITIVE
   integer, and a reply budget's deadline arithmetic (`PortaBridge>>armBudget`:
   deadline := now + budget, which the held loop reads the clock against) stays
   correct across the band edge.

   Before the fix the prim was TAG_SMI((long)ms) with no range check: the bit
   above the SMI payload shifted into the sign bit, so the clock went NEGATIVE
   at 2^30 ms (12 d 10 h) on the 32-bit C6, and a deadline computed just before
   the flip was never reached — then an unanswered leg spun in the interpreter
   (the old awaitReply: loop) until the observer rebooted the node as a wedge.

   The band edge is 2^62 on this 64-bit host and 2^30 on the target; the prim is
   the same code, so pushing the HOST clock past ITS edge exercises the one
   mechanism the fix adds (box what does not fit). Two advances (each an SMI,
   since advanceMillis: takes an SMI) park the clock 1000 ms BEFORE the host
   edge, the deadline is computed there, and the clock is then walked ACROSS
   the edge — the straddle a held loop's budget performs once per 49.7 days on
   a C6. Host-only: the virtual clock starts at 0 and only advanceMillis: moves
   it (timer_posix.c). *)
class MonotonicMillisBand packageUsing: manifest = () (
public main: platform args: args = (
  | t0 deadline t1 t2 |
  platform advanceMillis: 2305843009213693952.   (* 2^61 *)
  platform advanceMillis: 2305843009213692952.   (* 2^61 - 1000 -> clock = 2^62 - 1000 *)
  t0:: platform monotonicMillis.
  deadline:: t0 + 2000.                          (* armBudget's shape; promotes past the band *)
  platform advanceMillis: 1000.
  t1:: platform monotonicMillis.                 (* clock = 2^62, exactly one past the band *)
  (t1 > 0) println.                              (* was negative *)
  (t1 < deadline) println.                       (* still inside the budget *)
  platform advanceMillis: 2000.
  t2:: platform monotonicMillis.
  (t2 >= deadline) println.                      (* the budget EXPIRES — was never reached *)
  (t2 - t0 = 3000) println.                      (* and the clock stayed a clock *)
  'done' println.
)
)
